{
  "info": {
    "name": "Arzikina API",
    "description": "Collection de test pour l'API de synchronisation Arzikina (server/api). Couvre les endpoints câblés à ce stade : authentification par token, pull/push incrémental sur `categories` (seule entité branchée pour l'instant — voir docs/sync/AUDIT-ET-ARCHITECTURE-SYNC.md, section 10).\n\nUtilisation :\n1. Ajuster la variable de collection `baseUrl` si besoin (par défaut : le serveur local du réseau LAN, port 2222).\n2. Lancer d'abord \"Auth > Login\" — le token reçu est automatiquement enregistré dans la variable de collection `token` (script de test), les requêtes suivantes l'utilisent sans copier-coller manuel.\n3. Un utilisateur de test doit déjà exister en base (voir le commentaire en tête de `api/auth/login.php` — pas d'endpoint d'inscription pour l'instant).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://192.168.49.1:2222/arzikina",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "token",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "userId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "lastPullServerTime",
      "value": "0",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Auth",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Login",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"identifier\": \"test\",\n  \"password\": \"test\",\n  \"deviceId\": \"postman-test-device\",\n  \"deviceLabel\": \"Postman\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login.php",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "auth", "login.php"]
            },
            "description": "Corps attendu : identifier (username ou email), password, deviceId/deviceLabel optionnels. Renvoie { token, userId, expiresAt }. Voir api/auth/login.php pour le SQL de création d'un utilisateur de test."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "    const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('token', body.token);",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('userId', body.userId);",
                  "    pm.test('Login OK — token recu', () => pm.expect(body.token).to.be.a('string'));",
                  "} else {",
                  "    pm.test('Login a echoue — voir le corps de la reponse', () => {",
                  "        pm.expect.fail(pm.response.text());",
                  "    });",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Sync",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Pull - categories",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{token}}" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/sync/pull.php?entity_type=categories&updated_after={{lastPullServerTime}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "sync", "pull.php"],
              "query": [
                { "key": "entity_type", "value": "categories" },
                { "key": "updated_after", "value": "{{lastPullServerTime}}" }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Pull incremental : renvoie les categories de l'utilisateur authentifie modifiees strictement apres `updated_after` (millis). Mettre `updated_after=0` pour un premier pull complet."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "    const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('lastPullServerTime', body.serverTime);",
                  "    pm.test('Pull OK', () => pm.expect(body.entities).to.be.an('array'));",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Push - categories (CREATE)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{token}}" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"entityType\": \"categories\",\n  \"operations\": [\n    {\n      \"operation\": \"CREATE\",\n      \"entity\": {\n        \"id\": \"{{$guid}}\",\n        \"name\": \"Test Postman\",\n        \"icon\": \"ic_category_default\",\n        \"colorArgb\": -16776961,\n        \"type\": \"EXPENSE\",\n        \"createdAt\": {{$timestamp}}000,\n        \"updatedAt\": {{$timestamp}}000\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/sync/push.php",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "sync", "push.php"]
            },
            "description": "Envoie une operation CREATE sur categories. `id` doit etre un UUID (voir {{$guid}}, variable dynamique Postman). `results[0].serverEntity` contient l'etat final cote serveur a appliquer localement."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
